extraction_notes: "Printed 119-120. EXPERIENCE: the `Nightbane Sorceror & Nightbane Mystic` ladder, printed 233, read off a render (class-renders/nb-nightbane-sorcerer-mystic-ladder-crop.png), stored as the lower bound of each band; stated on this O.C.C. and not on the Nightbane R.C.C. per survey D2. RACE: restricted to `nb-nightbane` (survey D2); that R.C.C. is not yet imported. Not supersedes_race: ability 6 says the character keeps all the natural powers of the Nightbane R.C.C., so this is training, not a transformation. SPELLS: the four lists are nb-mystic''s, unchanged (see its notes for the 131 names, every spelling resolved, and Summon Entity, which has no row). Five from levels 1-2 at first level, four from 1-3 at second, two from 1-4 at third, and from fourth level one per level from any level up to the mystic''s own, stored as `all-invocations` plus `spell_levels: up_to_character_level` (BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT F61). The human Mystic''s outlook-shapes-the-spells paragraph and its `not likely to read symbols, runes or perform rituals` are NOT printed for this O.C.C. and are not stored. PSIONICS: none - printed 119 says Nightbane have no psionic potential whatsoever; no psionics block, stated as an ability and a restriction. SAVES: `+1 to save versus psychic attacks` is psionics: 1; +2 vs horror factor; `+1 to save vs magic` at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12 is stored as both spell_magic and ritual_magic, as nb-mystic stores the identical line. Spell strength has no sheet field: it is the Spell Strength ability and level_progression. P.P.E.: printed 119 says it is `the same as that of all members of his race. 3D6x10+20 plus the P.E. attribute. Add 2D6+6 per level of experience`. Stored as printed. The Nightbane R.C.C. itself prints P.E. plus 3D6x10+20, +3D6 per level (printed 88), so the two printings disagree on the per-level gain; which one a paired character receives is for the R.C.C. import to settle, and is not decided here. TALENTS: one at first level and one at levels 3, 7, 11 and 15, more bought with P.P.E. (`seldom more than one or two`). This replaces the R.C.C.''s free progression rather than adding to it, so it is the `Nightbane Talents (Mystic)` ability and level_progression, prose only; no talents block. MORPHUS/FACADE: the hand to hand bought with related picks affects the Facade only and the Morphus instinctively knows martial arts - prose in the related-skill note and restrictions. SKILLS: the O.C.C. skill list is Read/Speak Native Language, one language (+10%), one Lore (+15%) and Dance (+10%) and nothing else - the human Mystic''s Domestic skill is NOT printed here (confirmed on a render of printed 120, where the list continues straight into the hand to hand paragraph). Read/Speak Native Language 98% is stored as Language: Native Tongue and Literacy: Native Language, both 98. Dance +10% is 40 as nb-mystic stores it. Related skills are seven, at least two Technical. This book files Wilderness Survival under Espionage (printed 48) and grants it there at +10%, as nb-mystic states it. Secondary skills: four. MONEY: the average mystic''s 2D6x100 cash is stored; the 1D6x1,000 in possessions is not cash and is not stored; the wealth-oriented alternative (2D4x1,000 cash, 4D6x10,000 possessions - NOT the human Mystic''s 4D4x1,000) is in GM Notes. EQUIPMENT: `Most mystics will own very little`, with no item named, so there is no equipment_starting. HIT POINTS AND S.D.C. are not printed on the entry; they are the Nightbane R.C.C.''s (printed 88) and printed 36''s 3D6 S.D.C."
---

## Lore

The Nightbane Mystic is the most common magic-practicing Nightbane, one of the
few with a natural understanding of the energies coursing from the Nightlands to
Earth. In many primitive or nature-oriented cultures, Nightbane were considered
"touched by the spirits", blessed with the power to become the living embodiment
of their totem spirits - perhaps why animal-like Morphi are most common among
the Nightbane of those cultures - and so were prime candidates to follow the path
of mystical revelation.

Unlike human mystics, Nightbane have no psionic potential at all. They rely on
their Talents to stay in tune with the world, and on intuition for their spells.

## GM Notes

**The wealth-oriented mystic.** Most mystics own very little. A few who pursue
wealth end up owning property, vehicles, equipment, and stocks and bonds, but
they are very rare now, because they were easily found and destroyed in the days
following Dark Day. Such a mystic starts with 2D4x1,000 dollars in cash and
4D6x10,000 in possessions (housing, vehicles and equipment) instead of the
average mystic''s 2D6x100 in cash and 1D6x1,000 in possessions.

**Facade and Morphus.** The hand to hand skill a Nightbane Mystic buys with
related skill picks applies to the Facade only. In Morphus form the character
instinctively knows the equivalent of hand to hand: martial arts.

**Talents.** Additional Talents can be bought with permanent P.P.E., but seldom
more than one or two ever are: it is not natural for a mystic to force matters.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nb-nightbane-mystic');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nb-nightbane-mystic';

